{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "airline_service_quality",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "disruption_handling_quality",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "How the airline handles disruptions (delays, cancellations) is a genuine aspect OF service quality — the service dimension during irregular operations."
    },
    {
      "name": "staff_behavior_tone",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The demeanor/tone of staff is a constitutive interpersonal aspect of service quality."
    },
    {
      "name": "crew_responsiveness",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Crew responsiveness is an aspect of service quality, but it overlaps heavily with staff_behavior_tone — both capture the human/staff-interaction dimension, weakening mutual exclusivity."
    },
    {
      "name": "customer_service_resolution",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "How service issues are resolved is an aspect of service quality, though it overlaps conceptually with disruption_handling_quality (both concern problem handling/resolution)."
    },
    {
      "name": "aircraft_type_mismatch",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "external_predictor",
      "rationale": "Whether the operated aircraft differs from the advertised one is an operational/product attribute that may PREDICT dissatisfaction but is not itself an aspect of service quality; it is external to the service-quality concept."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": [
    "disruption_handling_quality",
    "staff_behavior_tone",
    "crew_responsiveness",
    "customer_service_resolution"
  ],
  "non_facet_columns": [
    "aircraft_type_mismatch"
  ],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.45,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.5,
  "rationale": "Four of five added columns are genuine facets of service quality, but the set skews heavily toward the human/staff and problem-handling dimensions. staff_behavior_tone and crew_responsiveness substantially overlap (both about staff interaction quality), and disruption_handling_quality and customer_service_resolution overlap (both about issue/problem resolution), lowering mutual exclusivity. Exhaustiveness is moderate-to-low because the tangible/physical service dimensions already present conceptually (seat comfort, food & beverage, inflight entertainment, cleanliness, boarding/check-in efficiency) are not represented among the added facets, so the decomposition covers only the interpersonal and disruption-handling slices of the concept. aircraft_type_mismatch is not a facet at all."
}
```

